    "summary": "Scorching desert set with killer China>Rider and epic Weather Report",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a smoking China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider and an explosive Eyes of the World → Weather Report Suite → Let It Grow sequence. Jerry’s guitar is “on fire” all night, while Keith’s organ adds depth to the suite. Overall it’s a top‑notch soundboard performance that captures the desert vibe perfectly.",
    "review": "On November 25, 1973 at Feyline Field in Tempe, AZ, the Dead turned the arid desert into a sonic oasis. From the opening “The Promised Land” through a tight first set, the band built momentum that exploded on the second‑set medley: a searing “Eyes Of The World” that locked in with Phil’s superb bass, segueing into the soaring “Weather Report Suite” (Prelude and Part 1) before bursting into a jubilant “Let It Grow.” The highlight for many listeners is the classic “China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider” jam where Jerry’s guitar was described as “on fire,” delivering slide‑filled solos that still sparkle. Keith’s organ tone on the suite was praised as perfect, adding lush layers to the improvisation, while Bill drove the energy with crisp, propulsive drumming. The encore, a gentle “And We Bid You Good Night,” closed the night with a warm desert sunset feel. All three SBD transfers are excellent, but the Sacks‑mastered version stands out as near‑perfect, offering crystal‑clear vocals and no tin‑can tape artifacts – truly top‑notch sound for one of ’73’s most memorable desert shows.",
